+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Image generation absent: gateway reserves provider slots but Studio has no image surface at all (Monica Gap 6/8) (bridge-20261027-audit-gap-image-gen)
+
+## Problem
+The Bangla feature audit (2026-10-27) mapped Monica's image/video generation as Gap 6. SupremeAI's gateway already reserves provider slots for image generation, and the platform's governance machinery (health-scored key routing, rate limiting, WORM audit trail, tenant namespacing) is fully operational and verified. But there is no image surface anywhere in Studio: no tab, no route, no API projection. A user cannot generate a single image.
+
+This is a governance-first product's dream feature to add: the expensive decisions (key custody, provider health, rate limiting, audit) are already solved platform-wide. What is missing is one provider wiring plus one tab.
+
+Deliberate scope line: images only in this wave. Video generation is deferred (slot reserved, provider economics unproven) — the audit does not treat video as launch-blocking for the "smart AI" perception, images it does.
+
+## Impact
+- Table stakes: for the home market and social sharing, "can it make me a picture" is a binary yes/no that dominates first impressions.
+- Consistency: when added informally (direct provider calls from scripts), image traffic would bypass key governance; doing it through the gateway keeps custody, health routing and audit uniform.
+- Growth: generated images are the most shareable artifact the product can produce — each share is an acquisition surface (pairs with the distribution-infrastructure gap, gap-08).
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Wire one image provider through the existing gateway (health-scored routing; key added to the platform's secret store by the operator — no keys in code or repo).
+2. Studio image tab: prompt input → generate → display; gallery of the user's last N generations; explicit content-policy note.
+3. Store generations under the tenant:user namespace with an audit-trail entry per generation (same discipline as every other action).
+4. Apply the platform's existing rate-limit pattern to generation requests.
+5. Provider outage path: honest typed error — no silent fallback, no fake placeholder images.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] End-to-end generation completes through gateway routing (no direct provider calls from the frontend — verifiable by absence of provider hostnames in network traffic)
+- [ ] Generated images are retrievable in the gallery across sessions, namespaced per tenant:user
+- [ ] Each generation writes an audit-trail entry
+- [ ] Rate limit enforced; exceeding it returns a typed, honest error
+- [ ] Provider outage produces a clear error state (no hang, no silent failure)
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** the platform's hardest problems (keys, health, limits, audit) are solved; this order only composes them into a new surface, and images are the most shareable output the product can offer.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) direct provider SDK calls from Studio — bypasses key custody, health routing and audit, creating a second ungoverned traffic class; (b) video generation first — highest cost and complexity with unproven provider economics; the reserved slot stays reserved; (c) a separate image microservice — no need, the gateway is the routing layer by design.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:studio` `area:gateway` `gap:monica-06`
